# The metric geometry of the hyperbolic plane, on the hyperboloid model of space/hyperbolic/hyperboloid (a point is x
# with B(x, x) = 1, cosh of a distance is B(x, y)). Every theorem is a polynomial identity proved for all real values.
# Where a theorem has hypotheses, it is stated as a CERTIFICATE: the difference of its two sides written as a sum of
# multiples of the hypotheses' differences. The kernel proves the certificate outright, and under the hypotheses every
# term vanishes, which is the theorem. (This is how a linear-combination tactic proves a conditional identity.)
#
#   CONGRUENCE     side-angle-side and side-side-side for two triangles, by one certificate;
#   THE TRIANGLE INEQUALITY   the Gram determinant of three vectors is det(x, y, z)^2. For points it reads
#                  (p^2 - 1)(q^2 - 1) - (r - p q)^2 = det^2 >= 0 with p, q, r the three cosh's, so
#                  cosh d(x, z) <= cosh(d(x, y) + d(y, z)), with equality exactly when det = 0;
#   COLLINEARITY   three points on one line have det = 0 (Cramer's identity), so for them the triangle inequality is
#                  an equality: one distance is the sum of the other two;
#   BETWEENNESS    for y = l x + m z, r B(y, y) - p q = l m (r^2 - B(x, x) B(z, z)): when y lies on the segment
#                  (l, m >= 0) the distances ADD, d(x, z) = d(x, y) + d(y, z), and between is additivity;
#   ISOMETRY CLASSES  a Mobius map of trace t has fixed points with discriminant t^2 - 4 (for determinant 1): two inside
#                  the half plane's closure as conjugates when t^2 < 4 (ELLIPTIC, a rotation), one double point at
#                  infinity when t^2 = 4 (PARABOLIC), two boundary points when t^2 > 4 (HYPERBOLIC, a translation);
#   THE CAYLEY MAP w = (z - i) / (z + i) carries the upper half plane onto the disk: 1 - |w|^2 = 4 Im z / |z + i|^2,
#                  and it scales differences by 2 i / ((z1 + i)(z2 + i)), so the two distance formulas agree;
#   THE ANGLE OF PARALLELISM  for a point at distance d from a line, the limiting parallel meets the perpendicular at
#                  the angle P with cos P = tanh d (Lobachevsky);
#   PASCH          a line crossing one side of a triangle crosses exactly one other (signs of B(., n));
#   AREA           the angle defect pi - (angle sum) is additive under cutting a triangle;
#   THE CIRCLE     a circle of radius r is traced at speed sinh r, so its circumference is 2 pi sinh r.

load @term/seed/space/hyperbolic/hyperboloid
  find lorentz-form
  find lorentz-cross-t
  find lorentz-cross-x
  find lorentz-cross-y

# CONGRUENCE, Hilbert's group III. For triangles (a, b, c) and (p, q, r), with the angle at a read as the tangent
# product angle(a) = B(b - B(b, a) a, c - B(c, a) a):
#
#   B(b, c) - B(q, r) = [angle(a) - angle(p)] + B(a, b) [B(a, c) - B(p, r)] + B(p, r) [B(a, b) - B(p, q)]
#                       - B(a, b) B(a, c) [B(a, a) - 1] + B(p, q) B(p, r) [B(p, p) - 1].
#
# SIDE-ANGLE-SIDE: if a and p are points and the triangles agree in the two sides at a and p and in the angle between
# them, every bracket is 0 and the third sides agree. SIDE-SIDE-SIDE: read for the angles, three equal sides make the
# angle difference 0.
rule side-angle-side-and-side-side-side
  mark a0, like integer
  mark a1, like integer
  mark a2, like integer
  mark b0, like integer
  mark b1, like integer
  mark b2, like integer
  mark c0, like integer
  mark c1, like integer
  mark c2, like integer
  mark p0, like integer
  mark p1, like integer
  mark p2, like integer
  mark q0, like integer
  mark q1, like integer
  mark q2, like integer
  mark r0, like integer
  mark r1, like integer
  mark r2, like integer
  show hold
    call is-equal
      call subtract
        call lorentz-form
          read b0
          read b1
          read b2
          read c0
          read c1
          read c2
        call lorentz-form
          read q0
          read q1
          read q2
          read r0
          read r1
          read r2
      call subtract
        call add
          call add
            call subtract
              call lorentz-form
                call subtract
                  read b0
                  call multiply
                    call lorentz-form
                      read b0
                      read b1
                      read b2
                      read a0
                      read a1
                      read a2
                    read a0
                call subtract
                  read b1
                  call multiply
                    call lorentz-form
                      read b0
                      read b1
                      read b2
                      read a0
                      read a1
                      read a2
                    read a1
                call subtract
                  read b2
                  call multiply
                    call lorentz-form
                      read b0
                      read b1
                      read b2
                      read a0
                      read a1
                      read a2
                    read a2
                call subtract
                  read c0
                  call multiply
                    call lorentz-form
                      read c0
                      read c1
                      read c2
                      read a0
                      read a1
                      read a2
                    read a0
                call subtract
                  read c1
                  call multiply
                    call lorentz-form
                      read c0
                      read c1
                      read c2
                      read a0
                      read a1
                      read a2
                    read a1
                call subtract
                  read c2
                  call multiply
                    call lorentz-form
                      read c0
                      read c1
                      read c2
                      read a0
                      read a1
                      read a2
                    read a2
              call lorentz-form
                call subtract
                  read q0
                  call multiply
                    call lorentz-form
                      read q0
                      read q1
                      read q2
                      read p0
                      read p1
                      read p2
                    read p0
                call subtract
                  read q1
                  call multiply
                    call lorentz-form
                      read q0
                      read q1
                      read q2
                      read p0
                      read p1
                      read p2
                    read p1
                call subtract
                  read q2
                  call multiply
                    call lorentz-form
                      read q0
                      read q1
                      read q2
                      read p0
                      read p1
                      read p2
                    read p2
                call subtract
                  read r0
                  call multiply
                    call lorentz-form
                      read r0
                      read r1
                      read r2
                      read p0
                      read p1
                      read p2
                    read p0
                call subtract
                  read r1
                  call multiply
                    call lorentz-form
                      read r0
                      read r1
                      read r2
                      read p0
                      read p1
                      read p2
                    read p1
                call subtract
                  read r2
                  call multiply
                    call lorentz-form
                      read r0
                      read r1
                      read r2
                      read p0
                      read p1
                      read p2
                    read p2
            call add
              call multiply
                call lorentz-form
                  read a0
                  read a1
                  read a2
                  read b0
                  read b1
                  read b2
                call subtract
                  call lorentz-form
                    read a0
                    read a1
                    read a2
                    read c0
                    read c1
                    read c2
                  call lorentz-form
                    read p0
                    read p1
                    read p2
                    read r0
                    read r1
                    read r2
              call multiply
                call lorentz-form
                  read p0
                  read p1
                  read p2
                  read r0
                  read r1
                  read r2
                call subtract
                  call lorentz-form
                    read a0
                    read a1
                    read a2
                    read b0
                    read b1
                    read b2
                  call lorentz-form
                    read p0
                    read p1
                    read p2
                    read q0
                    read q1
                    read q2
          call multiply
            call multiply
              call lorentz-form
                read p0
                read p1
                read p2
                read q0
                read q1
                read q2
              call lorentz-form
                read p0
                read p1
                read p2
                read r0
                read r1
                read r2
            call subtract
              call lorentz-form
                read p0
                read p1
                read p2
                read p0
                read p1
                read p2
              code 1
        call multiply
          call multiply
            call lorentz-form
              read a0
              read a1
              read a2
              read b0
              read b1
              read b2
            call lorentz-form
              read a0
              read a1
              read a2
              read c0
              read c1
              read c2
          call subtract
            call lorentz-form
              read a0
              read a1
              read a2
              read a0
              read a1
              read a2
            code 1

# The determinant of three vectors by Sarrus' rule, and of a symmetric 3 x 3 matrix with diagonal (a, g, c) and
# off-diagonal p (row 1 col 2), r (row 1 col 3), q (row 2 col 3).
task coordinate-determinant
  take x0, like integer
  take x1, like integer
  take x2, like integer
  take y0, like integer
  take y1, like integer
  take y2, like integer
  take z0, like integer
  take z1, like integer
  take z2, like integer
  like integer
  send back
    call subtract
      call add
        call add
          call multiply
            read x0
            call multiply
              read y1
              read z2
          call multiply
            read x1
            call multiply
              read y2
              read z0
        call multiply
          read x2
          call multiply
            read y0
            read z1
      call add
        call add
          call multiply
            read x2
            call multiply
              read y1
              read z0
          call multiply
            read x1
            call multiply
              read y0
              read z2
        call multiply
          read x0
          call multiply
            read y2
            read z1

task gram-determinant
  take ga, like integer
  take gg, like integer
  take gc, like integer
  take gp, like integer
  take gq, like integer
  take gr, like integer
  like integer
  send back
    call subtract
      call add
        call multiply
          read ga
          call multiply
            read gg
            read gc
        call multiply
          code 2
          call multiply
            read gp
            call multiply
              read gq
              read gr
      call add
        call add
          call multiply
            read ga
            call multiply
              read gq
              read gq
          call multiply
            read gg
            call multiply
              read gr
              read gr
        call multiply
          read gc
          call multiply
            read gp
            read gp

# THE GRAM DETERMINANT of three vectors under B is det(x, y, z)^2 (det J = 1), for all vectors.
rule the-gram-determinant-is-the-square-of-the-determinant
  mark x0, like integer
  mark x1, like integer
  mark x2, like integer
  mark y0, like integer
  mark y1, like integer
  mark y2, like integer
  mark z0, like integer
  mark z1, like integer
  mark z2, like integer
  show hold
    call is-equal
      call gram-determinant
        call lorentz-form
          read x0
          read x1
          read x2
          read x0
          read x1
          read x2
        call lorentz-form
          read y0
          read y1
          read y2
          read y0
          read y1
          read y2
        call lorentz-form
          read z0
          read z1
          read z2
          read z0
          read z1
          read z2
        call lorentz-form
          read x0
          read x1
          read x2
          read y0
          read y1
          read y2
        call lorentz-form
          read y0
          read y1
          read y2
          read z0
          read z1
          read z2
        call lorentz-form
          read x0
          read x1
          read x2
          read z0
          read z1
          read z2
      call multiply
        call coordinate-determinant
          read x0
          read x1
          read x2
          read y0
          read y1
          read y2
          read z0
          read z1
          read z2
        call coordinate-determinant
          read x0
          read x1
          read x2
          read y0
          read y1
          read y2
          read z0
          read z1
          read z2

# THE TRIANGLE INEQUALITY. For three points, with p = cosh d(x, y), q = cosh d(y, z), r = cosh d(x, z):
# (p^2 - 1)(q^2 - 1) - (r - p q)^2 = det(x, y, z)^2 >= 0, so r <= p q + sqrt((p^2 - 1)(q^2 - 1)) = cosh(d(x, y) + d(y, z)),
# and d(x, z) <= d(x, y) + d(y, z) since cosh increases on [0, oo). Equality exactly when det = 0.
rule the-triangle-inequality
  mark x0, like integer
  mark x1, like integer
  mark x2, like integer
  mark y0, like integer
  mark y1, like integer
  mark y2, like integer
  mark z0, like integer
  mark z1, like integer
  mark z2, like integer
  have x-point
    call is-equal
      call lorentz-form
        read x0
        read x1
        read x2
        read x0
        read x1
        read x2
      code 1
  have y-point
    call is-equal
      call lorentz-form
        read y0
        read y1
        read y2
        read y0
        read y1
        read y2
      code 1
  have z-point
    call is-equal
      call lorentz-form
        read z0
        read z1
        read z2
        read z0
        read z1
        read z2
      code 1
  show hold
    call is-equal
      call subtract
        call multiply
          call subtract
            call multiply
              call lorentz-form
                read x0
                read x1
                read x2
                read y0
                read y1
                read y2
              call lorentz-form
                read x0
                read x1
                read x2
                read y0
                read y1
                read y2
            code 1
          call subtract
            call multiply
              call lorentz-form
                read y0
                read y1
                read y2
                read z0
                read z1
                read z2
              call lorentz-form
                read y0
                read y1
                read y2
                read z0
                read z1
                read z2
            code 1
        call multiply
          call subtract
            call lorentz-form
              read x0
              read x1
              read x2
              read z0
              read z1
              read z2
            call multiply
              call lorentz-form
                read x0
                read x1
                read x2
                read y0
                read y1
                read y2
              call lorentz-form
                read y0
                read y1
                read y2
                read z0
                read z1
                read z2
          call subtract
            call lorentz-form
              read x0
              read x1
              read x2
              read z0
              read z1
              read z2
            call multiply
              call lorentz-form
                read x0
                read x1
                read x2
                read y0
                read y1
                read y2
              call lorentz-form
                read y0
                read y1
                read y2
                read z0
                read z1
                read z2
      call multiply
        call coordinate-determinant
          read x0
          read x1
          read x2
          read y0
          read y1
          read y2
          read z0
          read z1
          read z2
        call coordinate-determinant
          read x0
          read x1
          read x2
          read y0
          read y1
          read y2
          read z0
          read z1
          read z2

# COLLINEARITY: Cramer's identity det(x, y, z) J n = B(x, n) (y x z) + B(y, n) (z x x) + B(z, n) (x x y). Three
# points on the line n make every B(., n) zero, so det(x, y, z) J n = 0 and det = 0: for collinear points the triangle
# inequality is an equality, one distance the sum of the other two.
rule three-points-on-a-line-have-zero-determinant-t
  mark x0, like integer
  mark x1, like integer
  mark x2, like integer
  mark y0, like integer
  mark y1, like integer
  mark y2, like integer
  mark z0, like integer
  mark z1, like integer
  mark z2, like integer
  mark n0, like integer
  mark n1, like integer
  mark n2, like integer
  show hold
    call is-equal
      call multiply
        call coordinate-determinant
          read x0
          read x1
          read x2
          read y0
          read y1
          read y2
          read z0
          read z1
          read z2
        read n0
      call add
        call add
          call multiply
            call lorentz-form
              read x0
              read x1
              read x2
              read n0
              read n1
              read n2
            call subtract
              call multiply
                read y1
                read z2
              call multiply
                read y2
                read z1
          call multiply
            call lorentz-form
              read y0
              read y1
              read y2
              read n0
              read n1
              read n2
            call subtract
              call multiply
                read z1
                read x2
              call multiply
                read z2
                read x1
        call multiply
          call lorentz-form
            read z0
            read z1
            read z2
            read n0
            read n1
            read n2
          call subtract
            call multiply
              read x1
              read y2
            call multiply
              read x2
              read y1

rule three-points-on-a-line-have-zero-determinant-x
  mark x0, like integer
  mark x1, like integer
  mark x2, like integer
  mark y0, like integer
  mark y1, like integer
  mark y2, like integer
  mark z0, like integer
  mark z1, like integer
  mark z2, like integer
  mark n0, like integer
  mark n1, like integer
  mark n2, like integer
  show hold
    call is-equal
      call multiply
        call coordinate-determinant
          read x0
          read x1
          read x2
          read y0
          read y1
          read y2
          read z0
          read z1
          read z2
        call subtract
          code 0
          read n1
      call add
        call add
          call multiply
            call lorentz-form
              read x0
              read x1
              read x2
              read n0
              read n1
              read n2
            call subtract
              call multiply
                read y2
                read z0
              call multiply
                read y0
                read z2
          call multiply
            call lorentz-form
              read y0
              read y1
              read y2
              read n0
              read n1
              read n2
            call subtract
              call multiply
                read z2
                read x0
              call multiply
                read z0
                read x2
        call multiply
          call lorentz-form
            read z0
            read z1
            read z2
            read n0
            read n1
            read n2
          call subtract
            call multiply
              read x2
              read y0
            call multiply
              read x0
              read y2

rule three-points-on-a-line-have-zero-determinant-y
  mark x0, like integer
  mark x1, like integer
  mark x2, like integer
  mark y0, like integer
  mark y1, like integer
  mark y2, like integer
  mark z0, like integer
  mark z1, like integer
  mark z2, like integer
  mark n0, like integer
  mark n1, like integer
  mark n2, like integer
  show hold
    call is-equal
      call multiply
        call coordinate-determinant
          read x0
          read x1
          read x2
          read y0
          read y1
          read y2
          read z0
          read z1
          read z2
        call subtract
          code 0
          read n2
      call add
        call add
          call multiply
            call lorentz-form
              read x0
              read x1
              read x2
              read n0
              read n1
              read n2
            call subtract
              call multiply
                read y0
                read z1
              call multiply
                read y1
                read z0
          call multiply
            call lorentz-form
              read y0
              read y1
              read y2
              read n0
              read n1
              read n2
            call subtract
              call multiply
                read z0
                read x1
              call multiply
                read z1
                read x0
        call multiply
          call lorentz-form
            read z0
            read z1
            read z2
            read n0
            read n1
            read n2
          call subtract
            call multiply
              read x0
              read y1
            call multiply
              read x1
              read y0

# BETWEENNESS IS ADDITIVITY. For y = l x + m z: r B(y, y) - p q = l m (r^2 - B(x, x) B(z, z)), with p = B(x, y),
# q = B(y, z), r = B(x, z). For points on the segment (B(y, y) = 1, l, m >= 0) the right side is >= 0, so r >= p q,
# which with the collinear equality (r - p q)^2 = (p^2 - 1)(q^2 - 1) makes r = cosh(d(x, y) + d(y, z)): the distance
# from x to z through y is the sum. Hilbert's II.1 (y between x and z exactly when between z and x) is the symmetry
# of this identity in (x, l) and (z, m).
rule between-is-additive
  mark x0, like integer
  mark x1, like integer
  mark x2, like integer
  mark z0, like integer
  mark z1, like integer
  mark z2, like integer
  mark lam, like integer
  mark mu, like integer
  show hold
    call is-equal
      call subtract
        call multiply
          call lorentz-form
            read x0
            read x1
            read x2
            read z0
            read z1
            read z2
          call lorentz-form
            call add
              call multiply
                read lam
                read x0
              call multiply
                read mu
                read z0
            call add
              call multiply
                read lam
                read x1
              call multiply
                read mu
                read z1
            call add
              call multiply
                read lam
                read x2
              call multiply
                read mu
                read z2
            call add
              call multiply
                read lam
                read x0
              call multiply
                read mu
                read z0
            call add
              call multiply
                read lam
                read x1
              call multiply
                read mu
                read z1
            call add
              call multiply
                read lam
                read x2
              call multiply
                read mu
                read z2
        call multiply
          call lorentz-form
            read x0
            read x1
            read x2
            call add
              call multiply
                read lam
                read x0
              call multiply
                read mu
                read z0
            call add
              call multiply
                read lam
                read x1
              call multiply
                read mu
                read z1
            call add
              call multiply
                read lam
                read x2
              call multiply
                read mu
                read z2
          call lorentz-form
            call add
              call multiply
                read lam
                read x0
              call multiply
                read mu
                read z0
            call add
              call multiply
                read lam
                read x1
              call multiply
                read mu
                read z1
            call add
              call multiply
                read lam
                read x2
              call multiply
                read mu
                read z2
            read z0
            read z1
            read z2
      call multiply
        call multiply
          read lam
          read mu
        call subtract
          call multiply
            call lorentz-form
              read x0
              read x1
              read x2
              read z0
              read z1
              read z2
            call lorentz-form
              read x0
              read x1
              read x2
              read z0
              read z1
              read z2
          call multiply
            call lorentz-form
              read x0
              read x1
              read x2
              read x0
              read x1
              read x2
            call lorentz-form
              read z0
              read z1
              read z2
              read z0
              read z1
              read z2

# ISOMETRY CLASSES. A fixed point of z -> (a z + b) / (c z + d) solves c z^2 + (d - a) z - b = 0, and the
# discriminant of that quadratic is (a + d)^2 - 4 (a d - b c), the trace squared minus four for a determinant-1 map.
rule a-mobius-fixed-point-solves-a-quadratic
  mark ma, like integer
  mark mb, like integer
  mark mc, like integer
  mark md, like integer
  mark z, like integer
  show hold
    call is-equal
      call subtract
        call add
          call multiply
            read ma
            read z
          read mb
        call multiply
          read z
          call add
            call multiply
              read mc
              read z
            read md
      call subtract
        code 0
        call subtract
          call add
            call multiply
              read mc
              call multiply
                read z
                read z
            call multiply
              call subtract
                read md
                read ma
              read z
          read mb

rule the-fixed-point-discriminant-is-the-trace-squared-minus-four
  mark ma, like integer
  mark mb, like integer
  mark mc, like integer
  mark md, like integer
  show hold
    call is-equal
      call add
        call multiply
          call subtract
            read md
            read ma
          call subtract
            read md
            read ma
        call multiply
          code 4
          call multiply
            read mb
            read mc
      call subtract
        call multiply
          call add
            read ma
            read md
          call add
            read ma
            read md
        call multiply
          code 4
          call subtract
            call multiply
              read ma
              read md
            call multiply
              read mb
              read mc

# THE CAYLEY MAP w = (z - i) / (z + i). (z1 - i)(z2 + i) - (z2 - i)(z1 + i) = 2 i (z1 - z2), so
# w1 - w2 = 2 i (z1 - z2) / ((z1 + i)(z2 + i)). And with z = x + i y, |z + i|^2 - |z - i|^2 = 4 y, so
# 1 - |w|^2 = 4 Im z / |z + i|^2: the upper half plane goes into the disk. Put together,
# 2 |w1 - w2|^2 / ((1 - |w1|^2)(1 - |w2|^2)) = |z1 - z2|^2 / (2 Im z1 Im z2): the disk's distance formula
# (space/hyperbolic/hyperboloid) becomes the half plane's, so the Cayley map is an isometry.
rule the-cayley-map-scales-differences
  mark z1, like integer
  mark z2, like integer
  mark i, like integer
  show hold
    call is-equal
      call subtract
        call multiply
          call subtract
            read z1
            read i
          call add
            read z2
            read i
        call multiply
          call subtract
            read z2
            read i
          call add
            read z1
            read i
      call multiply
        call multiply
          code 2
          read i
        call subtract
          read z1
          read z2

rule the-cayley-map-sends-the-half-plane-into-the-disk
  mark u, like integer
  mark v, like integer
  show hold
    call is-equal
      call subtract
        call add
          call multiply
            read u
            read u
          call multiply
            call add
              read v
              code 1
            call add
              read v
              code 1
        call add
          call multiply
            read u
            read u
          call multiply
            call subtract
              read v
              code 1
            call subtract
              read v
              code 1
      call multiply
        code 4
        read v

# THE ANGLE OF PARALLELISM. Put the point at o = (1, 0, 0) and the line at distance d with normal
# n = (sinh d, cosh d, 0): a line (B(n, n) = -1), at distance d (B(o, n) = sinh d). The perpendicular from o is the line
# (0, 0, 1). A line through o has normal (0, cos t, sin t), and it is the limiting parallel when B(m, n)^2 = 1, that is
# cosh^2 d cos^2 t = 1. Then the angle P it makes with the perpendicular has cos P = |B(m, m_perp)| = |sin t|, and
# cosh^2 d sin^2 t = sinh^2 d: cos P = tanh d, Lobachevsky's formula (equivalently tan(P / 2) = e^-d).
rule the-line-at-distance-d-is-a-line
  mark ch, like integer
  mark sh, like integer
  have hyperbolic-unit
    call is-equal
      call subtract
        call multiply
          read ch
          read ch
        call multiply
          read sh
          read sh
      code 1
  show hold
    call is-equal
      call lorentz-form
        read sh
        read ch
        code 0
        read sh
        read ch
        code 0
      code -1

rule the-point-is-at-distance-d-from-the-line
  mark ch, like integer
  mark sh, like integer
  show hold
    call is-equal
      call lorentz-form
        code 1
        code 0
        code 0
        read sh
        read ch
        code 0
      read sh

rule the-perpendicular-from-the-point-meets-the-line-at-right-angles
  mark ch, like integer
  mark sh, like integer
  show hold
    call is-equal
      call lorentz-form
        code 0
        code 0
        code 1
        read sh
        read ch
        code 0
      code 0

rule the-perpendicular-passes-through-the-point
  show hold
    call is-equal
      call lorentz-form
        code 0
        code 0
        code 1
        code 1
        code 0
        code 0
      code 0

# The certificate: cosh^2 d sin^2 t - sinh^2 d = cosh^2 d [sin^2 t + cos^2 t - 1] - [cosh^2 d cos^2 t - 1]
# + [cosh^2 d - sinh^2 d - 1]. Under the three hypotheses (unit direction, limiting, cosh^2 - sinh^2 = 1) every bracket
# is 0, so cosh^2 d sin^2 t = sinh^2 d and cos P = |sin t| = tanh d.
rule lobachevsky-cos-of-the-angle-of-parallelism-is-tanh-d
  mark ch, like integer
  mark sh, like integer
  mark co, like integer
  mark si, like integer
  show hold
    call is-equal
      call subtract
        call multiply
          call multiply
            read ch
            read ch
          call multiply
            read si
            read si
        call multiply
          read sh
          read sh
      call add
        call subtract
          call multiply
            call multiply
              read ch
              read ch
            call subtract
              call add
                call multiply
                  read si
                  read si
                call multiply
                  read co
                  read co
              code 1
          call subtract
            call multiply
              call multiply
                read ch
                read ch
              call multiply
                read co
                read co
            code 1
        call subtract
          call subtract
            call multiply
              read ch
              read ch
            call multiply
              read sh
              read sh
          code 1

# THE CIRCLE OF RADIUS r about o: x(f) = (cosh r, sinh r cos f, sinh r sin f), on the plane, at distance r from o.
# Its velocity (0, -sinh r sin f, sinh r cos f) has squared length -B = sinh^2 r: it is traced at speed sinh r, so its
# circumference is 2 pi sinh r (and a disk's area, the integral of that, is 2 pi (cosh r - 1)).
rule a-circle-of-radius-r-lies-on-the-plane
  mark cr, like integer
  mark sr, like integer
  mark co, like integer
  mark si, like integer
  have hyperbolic-unit
    call is-equal
      call subtract
        call multiply
          read cr
          read cr
        call multiply
          read sr
          read sr
      code 1
  have unit-direction
    call is-equal
      call add
        call multiply
          read co
          read co
        call multiply
          read si
          read si
      code 1
  show hold
    call is-equal
      call lorentz-form
        read cr
        call multiply
          read sr
          read co
        call multiply
          read sr
          read si
        read cr
        call multiply
          read sr
          read co
        call multiply
          read sr
          read si
      code 1

rule a-circle-of-radius-r-is-at-distance-r
  mark cr, like integer
  mark sr, like integer
  mark co, like integer
  mark si, like integer
  show hold
    call is-equal
      call lorentz-form
        code 1
        code 0
        code 0
        read cr
        call multiply
          read sr
          read co
        call multiply
          read sr
          read si
      read cr

rule a-circle-is-traced-at-speed-sinh-r
  mark sr, like integer
  mark co, like integer
  mark si, like integer
  have unit-direction
    call is-equal
      call add
        call multiply
          read co
          read co
        call multiply
          read si
          read si
      code 1
  show hold
    call is-equal
      call subtract
        code 0
        call lorentz-form
          code 0
          call subtract
            code 0
            call multiply
              read sr
              read si
          call multiply
            read sr
            read co
          code 0
          call subtract
            code 0
            call multiply
              read sr
              read si
          call multiply
            read sr
            read co
      call multiply
        read sr
        read sr

# ORDER: PASCH'S AXIOM. A point of the segment from a to b is l a + m b with l, m > 0, and its side of the line n is
# B(l a + m b, n) = l B(a, n) + m B(b, n). So the segment crosses the line exactly when B(a, n) and B(b, n) have
# opposite signs (the sign of B(x, n) is the side of n the point x is on).
rule a-point-of-a-segment-sits-between-its-ends-sides
  mark a0, like integer
  mark a1, like integer
  mark a2, like integer
  mark b0, like integer
  mark b1, like integer
  mark b2, like integer
  mark n0, like integer
  mark n1, like integer
  mark n2, like integer
  mark lam, like integer
  mark mu, like integer
  show hold
    call is-equal
      call lorentz-form
        call add
          call multiply
            read lam
            read a0
          call multiply
            read mu
            read b0
        call add
          call multiply
            read lam
            read a1
          call multiply
            read mu
            read b1
        call add
          call multiply
            read lam
            read a2
          call multiply
            read mu
            read b2
        read n0
        read n1
        read n2
      call add
        call multiply
          read lam
          call lorentz-form
            read a0
            read a1
            read a2
            read n0
            read n1
            read n2
        call multiply
          read mu
          call lorentz-form
            read b0
            read b1
            read b2
            read n0
            read n1
            read n2

# The three side products multiply to a square: (ab)(ac)(bc) = (abc)^2 >= 0, writing ab = B(a, n) B(b, n) and so on.
# If the line crosses side ab (ab < 0) and misses c (c not on it), then (ac)(bc) <= 0 with neither zero, so exactly one
# of the sides ac, bc is crossed: a line entering a triangle through one side leaves through exactly one other.
rule pasch
  mark a0, like integer
  mark a1, like integer
  mark a2, like integer
  mark b0, like integer
  mark b1, like integer
  mark b2, like integer
  mark c0, like integer
  mark c1, like integer
  mark c2, like integer
  mark n0, like integer
  mark n1, like integer
  mark n2, like integer
  show hold
    call is-equal
      call multiply
        call multiply
          call lorentz-form
            read a0
            read a1
            read a2
            read n0
            read n1
            read n2
          call lorentz-form
            read b0
            read b1
            read b2
            read n0
            read n1
            read n2
        call multiply
          call multiply
            call lorentz-form
              read a0
              read a1
              read a2
              read n0
              read n1
              read n2
            call lorentz-form
              read c0
              read c1
              read c2
              read n0
              read n1
              read n2
          call multiply
            call lorentz-form
              read b0
              read b1
              read b2
              read n0
              read n1
              read n2
            call lorentz-form
              read c0
              read c1
              read c2
              read n0
              read n1
              read n2
      call multiply
        call multiply
          call multiply
            call lorentz-form
              read a0
              read a1
              read a2
              read n0
              read n1
              read n2
            call lorentz-form
              read b0
              read b1
              read b2
              read n0
              read n1
              read n2
          call lorentz-form
            read c0
            read c1
            read c2
            read n0
            read n1
            read n2
        call multiply
          call multiply
            call lorentz-form
              read a0
              read a1
              read a2
              read n0
              read n1
              read n2
            call lorentz-form
              read b0
              read b1
              read b2
              read n0
              read n1
              read n2
          call lorentz-form
            read c0
            read c1
            read c2
            read n0
            read n1
            read n2

# AREA. Cut a triangle with angles alpha, beta, gamma by a segment from the vertex at beta to the opposite side: the
# angle beta splits as beta1 + beta2 and the two angles at the foot add to pi (delta1 + delta2 = pi). Then the defects
# (pi minus the angle sum) of the two pieces add to the defect of the whole, plus (delta1 + delta2 - pi), which is 0:
# the defect is additive, and it is invariant under isometries (they keep angles), which are the defining properties of
# an area. Up to scale it is the hyperbolic area (Gauss-Bonnet, curvature -1).
rule the-angle-defect-is-additive
  mark alpha, like integer
  mark beta-one, like integer
  mark beta-two, like integer
  mark gamma, like integer
  mark delta-one, like integer
  mark delta-two, like integer
  mark pi, like integer
  mark beta, like integer
  have split-angle
    call is-equal
      read beta
      call add
        read beta-one
        read beta-two
  show hold
    call is-equal
      call add
        call subtract
          read pi
          call add
            call add
              read alpha
              read beta-one
            read delta-one
        call subtract
          read pi
          call add
            call add
              read gamma
              read beta-two
            read delta-two
      call subtract
        call subtract
          read pi
          call add
            call add
              read alpha
              read beta
            read gamma
        call subtract
          call add
            read delta-one
            read delta-two
          read pi

